import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="Configuration" description="Configure Hologram Live server, client, tracing, telemetry, modules, and update behavior.">
  <h1>Configuration</h1>
  <p>All platforms use <code>~/.config/hologram/live.toml</code>. The schema is typed, versioned, and rejects unknown fields.</p>

  <h2>Representative configuration</h2>
  <pre><code>schema_version = 2
role = "node"

[server]
listen = "127.0.0.1:11435"
max_rpc_bytes = 33554432
max_http_body_bytes = 33554432
graceful_shutdown_secs = 30
actor_mailbox_capacity = 128

[client]
preference = "local"
local_endpoint = "http://127.0.0.1:11435"
allow_read_fallback = true
request_timeout_secs = 30

[auth]
required = false
token_env = "HOLOGRAM_AUTH_TOKEN"

[tracing]
filter = "info,hologram_live=debug"
format = "pretty"
include_target = true
include_thread_ids = false

[telemetry]
enabled = true
service_name = "hologram-live"
export_timeout_secs = 5</code></pre>
  <p>Version 1 configurations are migrated automatically. Installations that used the original default module set gain the built-in echo chat module; customized module selections remain unchanged.</p>
  <div class="note"><strong>Telemetry remains local by default</strong>Leave <code>telemetry.endpoint</code> unset to prevent any telemetry network connection.</div>

  <h2>Environment overrides</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Configuration</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>HOLOGRAM_CONFIG</code></td><td>Explicit configuration file used by the CLI.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>HOLOGRAM_LISTEN</code></td><td>Server listen address.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>HOLOGRAM_REMOTE_ENDPOINT</code></td><td>Remote client authority.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>HOLOGRAM_LOG</code> / <code>RUST_LOG</code></td><td>Tracing filter.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT</code></td><td>OTLP/gRPC collector endpoint.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>OTEL_SERVICE_NAME</code></td><td>Telemetry service identity.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Remote safety</h2>
  <p>A non-loopback server listener requires authentication. Non-loopback client endpoints require HTTPS. Authentication, authorization, TLS, and integrity failures never trigger fallback to a different authority.</p>
</DocsLayout>
